          "recorded_role": "tool_result",
          "role": "tool_result",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"stdout\\\": \\\"332:\\\\\\\\subsection{Cross-Architecture, Cross-Scale, and Cross-Domain Generalization}\\\\n342:\\\\\\\\caption{Generalization of lead-lag detectability across architecture, scale, and domain ($\\\\\\\\alpha{=}1.0$, $n_{\\\\\\\\text{perm}}{=}5{,}000$). Each cell reports the fraction of canary$\\\\\\\\to$downstream pairs reaching significance (8~pairs per condition). Significance at permutation $p{<}0.05$; cross-method consensus ($K{\\\\\\\\geq}4/5$) serves as multiplicity control (see Appendix~\\\\\\\\ref{sec:fdr_sensitivity} for sensitivity analysis). Architecture conditions use a single seed; Scale and Domain conditions include two seeds (s42, s43) to assess replicability.}\\\\n351:Scale ($3.4\\\\\\\\times$) & Pythia-1.4B / Wiki (s42) & 7/8 & 6/8 & 8/8 & 5/8 & 0/8 & 0/8 & 5/8 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n352:Scale ($3.4\\\\\\\\times$) & Pythia-1.4B / Wiki (s43) & 8/8 & 6/8 & 8/8 & 6/8 & 2/8 & 4/8 & 6/8 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n369:Toda--Yamamoto ranges from 4/8 (Pythia-410M) to 6/8 (OPT-1.3B), with GPT-2-medium at 5/8; cross-architecture TY consistency contrasts with TY instability under Scale and Domain conditions (\\\\\\\\S\\\\\\\\ref{sec:consensus_validation}).\\\\n372:\\\\\\\\paragraph{Scale generalization.}\\\\n\\\", \\\"stderr\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"return_code\\\": 0}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {\\\"elapsed_seconds\\\": 0.51}}\"}"
